  "title": "Tahirih (Qurrat al-Ayn)",
  "summary": "Tahirih, also known as Qurrat al-Ayn, was a poet and preacher from Qazvin who became a leading follower of the Bab, as one of the Letters of the Living. She is said to have preached without a veil at the Badasht conference in 1848, was arrested and held in Tehran, and was put to death there in August 1852.",
